{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/806333-doubting-souls-doubts-and-questions","id":806333,"title":"Doubting Souls... doubts... and questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-11T12:38:01-08:00","id":806333,"title":"Doubting Souls... doubts... and questions","content":"I'm about to start a Doubting Souls game and, having received half of my players characters sheets and concepts, I have some questions, and some doubts on how to apply some things.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first is about Professions. There are some professions these players are interested that don't exist these days, so we had to create. I need opinions and suggestions.<br /> <br /> Alchemist - Probably rare those days still. We agreed on Science and Medicine as Asset skills.<br /> <br /> Inquisition Executioner - I think the players mostly wants something that uses Melee as asset skill. The other is Intimidation. And ruthless efficiency (sorry). I'm not sure about this. I think melee should be a Soldier? A knight, perhaps? As Profession, that is.<br /> <br /> So, this second character concept I'm having a bit of trouble with. Not because I'm against something, but on how to tie it to Salem. The players idea is to create a more physical character, because he never done one before. He is an inquisitor, an english knight and uses plate mail, a horse and spear and shield.<br /> <br /> Which seems nice, but feels to me something more of a few centuries behind. However, I think there are still knights like this in england up to the 19th century? Or somewhere in europe? Perhaps not a full body armor, but using a cuirass. I think shields aren't used anymore, though. And mounted knights with spears are probably still a thing, thought most soldiers would fire muskets at him.<br /> <br /> Also, can a knight be an inquisitor?<br /> <br /> And in Salem, if this concept is doable. I think the Salem people would probably look at someone like this with a bit of disgust and fear? Which is totally fine, by the way.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble researching those kinds of things, so any help is appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:15:11-08:00","id":806393,"title":"","content":"I'd say Apothecary is slightly more relevent than Alchemist for the time period. Inquisition Executioner also feels much more medieval than the era we're dealing with; Melee/Intimidation is a fine pair for something as simple as Thug or perhaps even Bounty Hunter.<br /> <br /> Plate armor has been on the decline for 300 years by the time of Doubting Souls; firearms have been relevent for long enough in warfare that heavy armor is largely phased out. Soldiers are going to look less like knights and more like Redcoats.<br /> <br /> Your players seem to be a bit caught up in the Middle Ages; remind them that they're much closer to the American Revolution and Golden Age of Piracy than they are to the Crusades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 01-11-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:37:16-08:00","id":806423,"title":"","content":"Or just show them best period piece for the <i>Doubting Souls</i> era - and about Witch near Salem ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gud8viI-P7Q\" data-code=\"gud8viI-P7Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/gud8viI-P7Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Plot takes place in 1630, but in those time it was more like &quot;just before&quot; Witch Trials of 1692-93. Just see the movie to get how much this is early modern era in contrast to Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> I plan to use it in my modern New England <b>Mage</b> chronicle, when I plan PCs to travel back in time to those events on story or two... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-11-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T14:30:48-08:00","id":806471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/806333-doubting-souls-doubts-and-questions?p=806393#post806393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Apothecary is slightly more relevent than Alchemist for the time period. Inquisition Executioner also feels much more medieval than the era we're dealing with; Melee/Intimidation is a fine pair for something as simple as Thug or perhaps even Bounty Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of this. Thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plate armor has been on the decline for 300 years by the time of Doubting Souls; firearms have been relevent for long enough in warfare that heavy armor is largely phased out. Soldiers are going to look less like knights and more like Redcoats. </div> </div> </div>The cuirass was used up to the 19th century, it seems. Mostly in France and Germany. But I don't see nothing of it's use in North America.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your players seem to be a bit caught up in the Middle Ages; remind them that they're much closer to the American Revolution and Golden Age of Piracy than they are to the Crusades. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. But I think these concepts can be updated to the era. I think it's possible to have a knight, with no armor and shield. I wanna know how well received it would be around Salem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/806333-doubting-souls-doubts-and-questions?p=806423#post806423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just show them best period piece for the <i>Doubting Souls</i> era - and about Witch near Salem ...<br /> <br /> Plot takes place in 1630, but in those time it was more like &quot;just before&quot; Witch Trials of 1692-93. Just see the movie to get how much this is early modern era in contrast to Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> I plan to use it in my modern New England <b>Mage</b> chronicle, when I plan PCs to travel back in time to those events on story or two... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis looks awesome! But isn't released yet, right? My main source of inspiration the Salem tv show, which I'm at the beginning of season 2. (Only two seasons so far). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T02:35:35-08:00","id":806857,"title":"","content":"If your player really wants an archaic crusader era knight my suggestion is to come up with a Hunter Conspiracy (or perhaps just the fading remains of one) who's Endowment suggests they use archaic weapons.<br /> <br /> The Aegis Kai Doru could do it - that armour is a Relic or the Malleus - that armour belonged to a crusader and grants bonuses to Benedictions. Even the Scarlet Watch might have a few Relics, as family heirlooms from the days when they were nobility. Though of course, they'd have to worry about a more powerful group trying to steal them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T12:47:18-08:00","id":807221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/806333-doubting-souls-doubts-and-questions#post806333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which seems nice, but feels to me something more of a few centuries behind. However, I think there are still knights like this in england up to the 19th century? Or somewhere in europe? Perhaps not a full body armor, but using a cuirass. I think shields aren't used anymore, though. And mounted knights with spears are probably still a thing, thought most soldiers would fire muskets at him.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're using knight to mean cavalry. By this time, they aren't the same thing anymore. A knight is a person with a particular title while cavalry are people who fight on horseback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T14:04:43-08:00","id":807281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/806333-doubting-souls-doubts-and-questions?p=806857#post806857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your player really wants an archaic crusader era knight my suggestion is to come up with a Hunter Conspiracy (or perhaps just the fading remains of one) who's Endowment suggests they use archaic weapons.<br /> <br /> The Aegis Kai Doru could do it - that armour is a Relic or the Malleus - that armour belonged to a crusader and grants bonuses to Benedictions. Even the Scarlet Watch might have a few Relics, as family heirlooms from the days when they were nobility. Though of course, they'd have to worry about a more powerful group trying to steal them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is very useful advice! Thank you! Now that you mention, those conspiracies do have anachronistic elements even in modern games. I think in the end the player came up with a new concept, but thinking like this there is a bit of leeway on what character concepts we can use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/806333-doubting-souls-doubts-and-questions?p=807221#post807221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're using knight to mean cavalry. By this time, they aren't the same thing anymore. A knight is a person with a particular title while cavalry are people who fight on horseback.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think you can still have a knight who uses a horse without being part of the cavalry, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:40:01-08:00","id":807687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/806333-doubting-souls-doubts-and-questions?p=807281#post807281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think you can still have a knight who uses a horse without being part of the cavalry, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uses in what sense? Lots of people use horses, they're the basic mode of transport. It's pretty unlikely someone with the status of a knighthood is going to be unable to ride a horse. If you mean, use as in 'is trained to fight on horseback' then, they're a cavalryman. You can certainly be both a cavalryman and also be a knight. They just aren't related anymore.<br /> <br /> My point basically is, if you want to update the concept of a knight, then you don't need them to be a literal knight. Just make them a soldier. Give them ride and weaponry as asset skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T08:10:35-08:00","id":807891,"title":"","content":"There's sample professions in our upcoming Doubting Souls chapter itself, but I want to point out that these aren't necessarily tied to Salem Town and Salem Village themselves. Really, it depends upon where the player-character comes from, how the PC came to be in Salem, and why. There might be a few legitimate anachronisms, however, since an apothecary in Boston would likely be different than one in Salem Town who could be relying on outdated methods or folklore. In other words, I wouldn't get hung up on the ideal version of a profession, since that will vary greatly. Instead, I'd tie it to the character's background so it makes sense for the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:02:29-08:00","id":808259,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the reply, Monica! Nice to know there will be sample professions there, too and I'm really excited to see what new things are in the chapter! Yeah, most of the PCs will be out of town, so it's easier to tie a profession and concept they come up with. Also, I don't like to block a concept without seeing if it's possible in some way and giving feedback on what could be changed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Btw, if anyone is curious. The knight player came up with a new concept, though. A former spy for the crown who joined the church and a personal/religious quest took him to Salem. Also, the one with the apothecary/alchemist profession is an Ascending One who wants to craft bombs and poisons. still working on the concept, probably someone from England or Istanbul.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T05:20:04-08:00","id":828739,"title":"","content":"Needed to share with you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/bJ5t1pf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}